			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["133E40031AC9FB97"]
			description: [
				"Search the compass for biomesoplenty entries. Pick a bright grassland, wetland, highland or colourful forest rather than accepting another dark oak forest."
				"Nature's Compass locates biomes but does not remove travel cost or chunk generation. Search deliberately, coordinate with other explorers, and stop once the team has a useful route rather than generating an enormous empty frontier."
				"The Cartographers call distant terrain a promise, not a consumable. Roads, ships, rails, and named outposts make exploration cumulative instead of turning each trip into another disconnected sprint."
				"Terralith shapes the large landforms; Biomes O' Plenty and smaller biome mods supply distinct plants, woods, and palettes. Several systems can influence one view, so identify the exact biome before guessing which mod made it."
			]
			id: "41EBD1EB56456B34"
			rewards: [{
				id: "116EC4D37A11B141"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 15
