		}
		{
			dependencies: ["41EBD1EB56456B34"]
			description: [
				"Lavender fields and other flower-rich regions add colour without changing survival progression. Collect a small sample and leave the landscape recognisable."
				"Bring saplings and a small renewable sample home, but leave the original ecosystem recognisable. A palette library is more useful than stripping every rare grove around its first waypoint."
				"Record biome name, coordinates, season, useful resources, hazards, and a screenshot or photograph. The same wood colour can come from different ecological stories and may have different nearby ingredients."
				"Nature's Compass locates biomes but does not remove travel cost or chunk generation. Search deliberately, coordinate with other explorers, and stop once the team has a useful route rather than generating an enormous empty frontier."
