		{
			dependencies: ["3A8709849D637D3D"]
			description: [
				"Exposure cameras use film and preserve in-world moments. Start with a camera and black-and-white film, then learn the viewfinder controls."
				"Exposure follows a complete film workflow: load compatible film, take exposures, remove the exposed roll, develop it in the Lightroom, then organise or copy the resulting photographs. Practise every step at home first."
				"Keep blank, exposed, and developed film in visibly separate storage. If the camera appears unresponsive, check loaded film, remaining frames, keybinds, and recipe compatibility before replacing the mod or resource pack."
				"A creative expedition should return with more than screenshots: develop an album, label an object, write the route, and explain one mechanic. Art becomes field knowledge when it helps the next player understand the place."
			]
			id: "5A57FC5CEB08D333"
			rewards: [{
				id: "71BE6BED6206C799"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 15
			}]
